>:<fpage>815</fpage>&#x02013;824.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9626657</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Li, L., H. Yuan, W. Xie, J. Mao, A.M. Caruso, A. McMahon, D.J. Sussman, and D. Wu. <year>1999</year>. Dishevelled proteins lead to two signaling pathways. Regulation of LEF-1 and c-Jun N-terminal kinase in mammalian cells. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>274(1)</volume>:<fpage>129</fpage>&#x02013;134.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9867820</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Liu, T., A.J. DeCostanzo, X. Liu, H. Wang, S. Hallagan, R.T. Moon, and C.C. Malbon. <year>2001</year>. G protein signaling from activated rat frizzled-1 to the &#x003b2;-catenin-Lef-Tcf pathway. <source>Science.</source> <volume>292</volume>:<fpage>1718</fpage>&#x02013;1722.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11387477</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Medina, A., W. Reintsch, and H. Steinbeisser. <year>2000</year>. <italic>Xenopus</italic> frizzled 7 can act in canonical and non-canonical Wnt signaling pathways: implications on early patterning and morphogenesis. <source>Mech. Dev.</source> <volume>92</volume>:<fpage>227</fpage>&#x02013;237.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10727861</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Mellor, H., and P.J. Parker. <year>1998</year>. The extended protein kinase C superfamily. <source>Biochem. J.</source> <volume>332</volume>:<fpage>281</fpage>&#x02013;292.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9601053</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Miller, J.R., A.M. Hocking, J.D. Brown, and R.T. Moon. <year>1999</year>. Mechanism and function of signal transduction by the Wnt/&#x003b2;-catenin and Wnt/Ca<sup>2+</sup> pathways. <source>Oncogene.</source> <volume>18</volume>:<fpage>7860</fpage>&#x02013;7872.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10630639</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Mudher, A., S. Chapman, J. Richardson, A. Asuni, G. Gibb, C. Pollard, R. Killick, T. Iqbal, L. Raymond, I. Varndell, et al. <year>2001</year>. Dishevelled regulates the metabolism of amyloid precursor protein via protein kinase C/mitogen-activated protein kinase and c-Jun terminal kinase. <source>J. Neurosci.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>4987</fpage>&#x02013;4995.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11438574</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Pandur, P., M. Lasche, L.M. Eisenberg, and M. Kuhl. <year>2002</year>. Wnt-11 activation of a non-canonical Wnt signalling pathway is required for cardiogenesis. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>418</volume>:<fpage>636</fpage>&#x02013;641.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12167861</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><citation citation-type="journal">Penton, A., A. Wodarz, and R. Nusse. <year>2002</year>. A mutational analysis of dishevelled in <italic>Drosophila</italic> defines novel domains in the dishevelled protein as well as novel supressing alleles of axin. <source>Genetics.</source> <volume>161</volume>:<fpage>747</fpage>&#x02013;762.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12072470</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib31"><citation citation-type="journal">Peifer, M., and D.G. McEwen. <year>2002</year>. The ballet of morphogenesis&#x0003b; unveiling the hideen choreographers. <source>Cell.</source> <volume>109</volume>:<fpage>271</fpage>&#x02013;274.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12015976</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib32"><citation citation-type="journal">Sheldahl, L.C., M. Park, C.C. Malbon, and R.T. Moon. <year>1999</year>. Protein kinase C is differentially stimulated by Wnt and Frizzled homologs in a G-protein-dependent manner. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>9</volume>:<fpage>695</fpage>&#x02013;698.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10395542</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib33"><citation citation-type="journal">Shulman, J.M., N. Perrimon, and J.D. Axelrod. <year>1998</year>. Frizzled signaling and the developmental control of cell polarity. <source>Trends Genet.</source> <volume>14</volume>:<fpage>452</fpage>&#x02013;458.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9825673</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib34"><citation citation-type="journal">Slusarski, D.C., and V.G. Corces. <year>2000</year>. Calcium imaging in cell-cell signaling. <source>Methods Mol. Biol.</source> <volume>135</volume>:<fpage>253</fpage>&#x02013;261.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10791322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib35"><citation citation-type="journal">Slusarski, D.C., V.G. Corces, and R.T. Moon. <year>1997</year>a. Interaction of Wnt and a Frizzled homologue triggers G-protein-linked phosphatidylinositol signalling. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>390</volume>:<fpage>410</fpage>&#x02013;413.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9389482</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib36"><citation citation-type="journal">Slusarski, D.C., J. Yang-Snyder, W.B. Busa, and R.T. Moon. <year>1997</year>b. Modulation of embryonic intracellular Ca<sup>2+</sup> signaling by Wnt-5A. <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>182</volume>:<fpage>114</fpage>&#x02013;120.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9073455</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib37"><citation citation-type="journal">Smith, J.C., F.L. Conlon, Y. Saka, and M. Tada. <year>2000</year>. Xwnt11 and the regulation of gastrulation in <italic>Xenopus</italic>. <source>Philos. Trans. R. Soc. Lond. B Biol. Sci.</source> <volume>355</volume>:<fpage>923</fpage>&#x02013;930.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11128985</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib38"><citation citation-type="journal">Tada, M., and J.C. Smith. <year>2000</year>. Xwnt11 is a target of <italic>Xenopus</italic> Brachyury: regulation of gastrulation movements via Dishevelled, but not through the canonical Wnt pathway. <source>Development.</source> <volume>127</volume>:<fpage>2227</fpage>&#x02013;2238.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10769246</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib39"><citation citation-type="journal">Torres, M.A., J.A. Yang-Snyder, S.M. Purcell, A.A. DeMarais, L.L. McGrew, and R.T. Moon. <year>1996</year>. Activities of the Wnt-1 class of secreted signaling factors are antagonized by the Wnt-5A class and by a dominant negative cadherin in early <italic>Xenopus</italic> development. <source>J. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>133</volume>:<fpage>1123</fpage>&#x02013;1137.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8655584</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib40"><citation citation-type="journal">Veeman, M.T., D.C. Slusarski, A. Kaykas, S. Hallagan, and R.T. Moon. <year>2003</year>. Zebrafish Prickle, a modulator of non-canonical Wnt/Fz signaling, regulates gastrulation movements. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>674</fpage>&#x02013;679.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12699625</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib41"><citation citation-type="journal">Wallingford, J.B., B.A. Rowning, K.M. Vogeli, U. Rothbacher, S.E. Fraser, and R.M. Harland. <year>2000</year>. Dishevelled controls cell polarity during <italic>Xenopus</italic> gastrulation. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>405</volume>:<fpage>81</fpage>&#x02013;85.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10811222</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib42"><citation citation-type="journal">Wallingford, J.B., S.E. Fraser, and R.M. Harland. <year>2002</year>. Convergent extension: the molecular control of polarized cell movement during embryonic development. <source>Dev. Cell.</source> <volume>2</volume>:<fpage>695</fpage>&#x02013;706.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12062082</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib43"><citation citation-type="journal">Wharton, K.A., Jr. <year>2003</year>. Runnin' with the Dvl: proteins that associate with Dsh/Dvl and their significance to Wnt signal transduction. <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>253</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;17.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12490194</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib44"><citation citation-type="journal">Winklbauer, R., A. Medina, R.K. Swain, and H. Steinbeisser. <year>2001</year>. Frizzled-7 signalling controls tissue separation during <italic>Xenopus</italic> gastrulation. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>413</volume>:<fpage>856</fpage>&#x02013;860.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11677610</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib45"><citation citation-type="journal">Yamanaka, H., T. Moriguchi, N. Masuyama, M. Kusakabe, H. Hanafusa, R. Takada, S. Takada, and E. Nishida. <year>2002</year>. JNK functions in the non-canonical Wnt pathway to regulate convergent extension movements in vertebrates. <source>EMBO Rep.</source> <volume>3</volume>:<fpage>69</fpage>&#x02013;75.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11751577</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib46"><citation citation-type="journal">Yang-Snyder, J., J.R. Miller, J.D. Brown, C.J. Lai, and R.T. Moon. <year>1996</year>. A frizzled homolog functions in a vertebrate Wnt signaling pathway. <source>Curr. Biol.</source> <volume>6</volume>:<fpage>1302</fpage>&#x02013;1306.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8939578</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib47"><citation citation-type="journal">Zhang, Y., S.Y. Neo, J. Han, and S.C. Lin. <year>2000</year>. Dimerization choices control the ability of axin and dishevelled to activate c-Jun N-terminal kinase/stress-activated protein kinase. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>275</volume>:<fpage>25008</fpage>&#x02013;25014.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10829020</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn id="fn1"><label>*</label><p>Abbreviations used in this paper: CamKII, calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase II&#x0003b; Dsh, Dishevelled&#x0003b; Fz, Frizzled&#x0003b; JNK, jun-N-terminal kinase&#x0003b; MO, morpholino&#x0003b; PCP, planar cell polarity&#x0003b; PTX, pertussis toxin&#x0003b; TnIc, cardiac troponin I&#x0003b; wt, wild type.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>